## Approach
Apply Kadane's Algorithm. Maintain running maximum sum ending at each position and update overall maximum sum encountered.

## Algorithm
Kadane's Dynamic Programming Algorithm

## Code
```c++
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <algorithm>

int maxSubArray(const std::vector<int>& nums) {
 int max_so_far = nums[0];
 int curr_max = nums[0];
 for (size_t i = 1; i < nums.size(); ++i) {
 curr_max = std::max(nums[i], curr_max + nums[i]);
 max_so_far = std::max(max_so_far, curr_max);
 }
 return max_so_far;
}

int main() {
 std::vector<int> nums = {-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4};
 std::cout << maxSubArray(nums) << std::endl;
 return 0;
}
```

